For risk stratification, a risk score was generated for each patient of the cohorts by scikit-survival’s “predict” method. Based on the predicted risk scores, a minimal P approach was used to identify the best cut-off value between the 25th and 75th percentile to divide the patients into high- and lowrisk groups. P values between the low- and high-risk groups
